From 6f16dc6afa161b7d80cd1899d5267784c3552445 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: razgulay <bantran09@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:18:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(translator): validate thought signatures upfront
 instead of eating a 400 retry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Multi-turn tool conversations carried stale or client-mangled
thoughtSignature values upstream — __ts__ payloads the client truncated,
space-mangled, or percent-encoded on the way back, plus expired store
entries that outlived a Google key rotation. Google answered 400
"Corrupted thought signature. INVALID_ARGUMENT" and only then did
proxy.ForwardGemini replace every signature with DefaultThinkingSignature
and replay, doubling latency on every corrupted turn.

TranslateOpenAIToGemini now shape-validates every signature before the
request leaves (base64-decodable, sane length) and signs unusable ones
with the known-accepted default immediately. Unsigned sibling calls are
defaulted too — first-call-only defaulting left them unsigned, and the
reactive retry's all-default replay is the proven-accepted shape. The
reactive retry stays as a last-resort safety net.
